```md
# Checkers (Draughts) Game
A fully functional Checkers game with graphical user interface implemented in Python using Pygame.
## Features
- 8x8 checkers board with standard starting positions
- Two-player alternating turns (Red vs White)
- Standard checkers movement rules
- Mandatory capture enforcement
- King piece promotion (crowned pieces)
- Multiple jumps in a single turn
- Visual highlighting of selected pieces and valid moves
- Game state tracking and win detection
- Move notation display
## Installation
1. Make sure you have Python 3.7 or higher installed
2. Install the required dependencies:
   ```
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```
3. Run the game:
   ```
   python main.py
   ```
## How to Play
1. Red pieces start at the top, White pieces at the bottom
2. Click on a piece to select it (valid moves will be highlighted in yellow)
3. Click on a highlighted square to move the selected piece
4. Captures are mandatory when available
5. Pieces become kings when they reach the opposite end of the board
6. Kings can move and capture both forward and backward
7. The game ends when one player captures all opponent pieces
```

