# Checkers (Draughts) Game - User Manual

## Overview
Welcome to the Checkers (Draughts) game! This is a fully functional implementation of the classic board game with a modern graphical interface. The game follows standard international draughts rules on an 8x8 board, featuring two-player gameplay, mandatory captures, king promotions, and multiple jumps.

## System Requirements
- **Operating System**: Windows 10/11, macOS 10.15+, or Linux (Ubuntu 18.04+)
- **Python Version**: Python 3.7 or higher
- **RAM**: Minimum 2GB
- **Display**: 800x800 resolution or higher

## Installation Guide

### Step 1: Install Python
If you don't have Python installed, download and install it from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).

### Step 2: Install Dependencies
Open your terminal or command prompt and run:

```bash
pip install pygame>=2.5.0
```

### Step 3: Download Game Files
Download the following files to the same directory:
- `main.py`
- `game.py`
- `gui.py`
- `requirements.txt` (optional, for reference)

## How to Play

### Starting the Game
1. Navigate to the directory containing the game files
2. Run the game using:
```bash
python main.py
```

### Game Interface
The game window consists of:
- **Game Board**: 8x8 alternating brown and beige squares
- **Turn Indicator**: Shows which player's turn it is (Red or White)
- **Piece Count**: Displays remaining pieces and kings for each player
- **Move Notation**: Shows selected piece coordinates
- **Capture Warning**: Alerts when mandatory captures are available

### Game Rules

#### Basic Movement
- **Red pieces** start at the top three rows and move downward
- **White pieces** start at the bottom three rows and move upward
- Regular pieces move diagonally forward one square
- Kings can move diagonally in any direction

#### Capturing
- **Mandatory Capture**: If a capture is available, you must take it
- **Multiple Jumps**: If additional captures are available after a jump, you must continue jumping
- **Capture Direction**: Pieces can jump forward over opponent pieces; kings can jump in any direction

#### King Promotion
- Red pieces become kings when reaching row 7 (bottom row)
- White pieces become kings when reaching row 0 (top row)
- Kings are marked with a yellow crown and can move in any diagonal direction

### Controls
- **Mouse Click**: Select pieces and make moves
- **Game Over**: Click anywhere to restart after a game ends
- **Window Close**: Click the X button or press Alt+F4 to exit

### Playing a Turn
1. **Select a Piece**: Click on one of your pieces (highlighted in green when selected)
2. **View Valid Moves**: Yellow squares indicate where you can move
3. **Make a Move**: Click on a yellow square to move your piece
4. **Multiple Jumps**: If you capture a piece and more captures are available, continue selecting the same piece

### Game End Conditions
The game ends when:
- One player has no pieces remaining
- A player cannot make any legal moves

The winner is displayed with a game over screen showing which color won.

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

#### 1. Pygame Installation Fails
```bash
# Try using pip3 instead of pip
pip3 install pygame

# Or on some systems
python -m pip install pygame
```

#### 2. Game Window Doesn't Open
- Ensure all game files are in the same directory
- Check Python version with `python --version`
- Verify Pygame installation with `python -c "import pygame; print(pygame.version.ver)"`

#### 3. Game Runs Slowly
- Close other applications to free up system resources
- Ensure your graphics drivers are up to date
- The game is optimized for 60 FPS; performance issues are rare on modern systems

#### 4. Font Display Issues
The game includes fallback fonts. If text appears incorrectly, it will use Pygame's default font automatically.

### Getting Help
If you encounter issues not covered here:
1. Check that you have the latest version of Python and Pygame
2. Ensure all game files are present and in the same folder
3. Restart your computer and try again
4. Contact support with a description of the issue and your system specifications

## Features in Detail

### Visual Features
- **Piece Highlighting**: Selected pieces glow green
- **Valid Move Indicators**: Available moves show as yellow squares
- **King Visualization**: Crowned pieces display a yellow crown
- **Capture Warnings**: Clear visual indication when captures are mandatory
- **Game State Display**: Real-time piece counts and turn information

### Game Logic Features
- **Complete Rule Enforcement**: All standard checkers rules implemented
- **Mandatory Capture Detection**: Automatic detection and enforcement
- **Multiple Jump Handling**: Seamless continuation of capture chains
- **King Promotion**: Automatic promotion when reaching opposite end
- **Win Detection**: Automatic game end detection and winner declaration

### User Experience Features
- **Intuitive Controls**: Simple click-to-move interface
- **Visual Feedback**: Clear indication of game state
- **One-Click Restart**: Easy game reset after completion
- **Performance Optimized**: Smooth 60 FPS gameplay

## Tips for Beginners
1. **Control the Center**: Pieces in the center have more movement options
2. **Create Kings Early**: Getting kings gives you more strategic options
3. **Force Captures**: Position your pieces to force opponent captures that benefit you
4. **Protect Your Back Row**: Keep pieces on your back row to prevent opponent kings
5. **Plan Multiple Jumps**: Look for opportunities to set up multiple captures in one turn

## Uninstallation
To remove the game:
1. Delete the game files from your computer
2. Optionally uninstall Pygame:
```bash
pip uninstall pygame
```

## Credits
This Checkers game was developed using Python and Pygame, implementing standard international draughts rules with a focus on user-friendly gameplay and visual clarity.

Enjoy your game of Checkers!

